======================================================================
TIGHT MECHANISM ANALYSIS (n=5)
======================================================================
At n=5: mu(C) = 1 for ALL odd cycles C through any vertex Q.
  Reason: T-v has 4 vertices. Any 3-cycle C's {C\{v}} avoids 2 vertices,
  leaving 2 vertices in T-v -- too few for odd cycles. So mu(3-cycle) = 1.
  For 5-cycle: C\{v} = 4 vertices = all of T-v. mu(5-cycle) = 1.
  For 7-cycle (not possible at n=5 -- max cycle length = n = 5).

Therefore at n=5: delta = 2 * c_odd(Q) where c_odd(Q) = #{odd cycles through Q}.
Tight (delta = 2|rivals|) iff c_odd(Q) = |rivals|.
Since c_odd(Q) >= |rivals| by King theorem, tight iff each rival in exactly 1 odd cycle with Q.

