  Result: FAILURES FOUND

When does mu(C) > 1 first appear?
  mu(C) > 1 requires: in T-v, exists an odd cycle avoiding C\{v}.
  For 3-cycle C=(v,a,b): need odd cycle in T-v avoiding {a,b}.
  T-v has n-1 vertices. Odd cycle avoiding {a,b} needs >= 3 remaining vertices.
  So n-1-2 = n-3 remaining vertices, need n-3 >= 3, i.e., n >= 6.
  At n=6: first possible mu(3-cycle) > 1.

For n=6: checking range of mu(3-cycles)...
  mu values for first tournament: []
  mu values for all n=6 tournaments: [1, 3]

